4dk|a|Depending on will or discretion; not governed by any fixed rules; as, an arbitrary decision; an arbitrary punishment. ; Exercised according to one's own will or caprice, and therefore conveying a notion of a tendency to abuse the possession of power. ; Despotic; absolute in power; bound by no law; harsh and unforbearing; tyrannical; as, an arbitrary prince or government.	j:1stb,59,5;1l55,47,4;1e95,39,4;1l4t,26,3~1stb,59,5;1l55,47,4;1e95,39,4;1l4t,26,3	e:1xo5,57,5~1xo5,57,5
4ej|n|A portion of a curved line; as, the arc of a circle or of an ellipse. ; A curvature in the shape of a circular arc or an arch; as, the colored arc (the rainbow); the arc of Hadley's quadrant. ; An arch. ; The apparent arc described, above or below the horizon, by the sun or other celestial body. The diurnal arc is described during the daytime, the nocturnal arc during the night.	a:nw1,96,4~nw1,96,4	N:2ab7,125,3;1urc,91,3;21bo,35,2~1urc,91,3;2ab7,125,3;21bo,35,2
